of the fluoroscopic image quality of a dynamic solid-state digital X-ray detector. Med Phys 28:11&#x02013;5 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11213916</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Granfors</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name><name><surname>Aufrichtig</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Possin</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Performance of a 41&#x000d7;41 cm<sup>2</sup> amorphous silicon flat panel X-ray detector designed for angiographic and R&#x00026;F imaging applications</article-title><source>Med Phys</source><year>2003</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>2715</fpage><lpage>2726</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1118/1.1609151</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Granfors PR, Aufrichtig R, Possin G, et al (2003) Performance of a 41&#x000d7;41 cm2 amorphous silicon flat panel x-ray detector designed for angiographic and R&#x00026;F imaging applications. Med Phys 30:2715&#x02013;726 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14596310</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hunt</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Tousignant</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Rowlands</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of the imaging properties of an amorphous selenium-based flat panel detector for digital fluoroscopy</article-title><source>Med Phys</source><year>2004</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>1166</fpage><lpage>1175</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1118/1.1707755</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Hunt DC, Tousignant O, Rowlands JA (2004) Evaluation of the imaging properties of an amorphous selenium-based flat panel detector for digital fluoroscopy. Med Phys 31:1166&#x02013;175 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15191306</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vano</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Geiger</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Schreiner</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Dynamic flat panel detector versus image intensifier in cardiac imaging: dose and image quality</article-title><source>Phys Med Biol</source><year>2005</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>5731</fpage><lpage>5742</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1088/0031-9155/50/23/022</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Vano E, Geiger B, Schreiner A, et al (2005) Dynamic flat panel detector versus image intensifier in cardiac imaging: dose and image quality. Phys Med Biol 50:5731&#x02013;742 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16306664</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhao</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Reznik</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Indirect flat-panel detector with avalanche gain: fundamental feasibility investigation for SHARP&#x02013;AMFPI (scintillator HARP active matrix flat panel imager)</article-title><source>Med Phys</source><year>2005</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>2954</fpage><lpage>2966</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1118/1.2008428</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Zhao W, Li D, Reznik A, et al (2005) Indirect flat-panel detector with avalanche gain: fundamental feasibility investigation for SHARP&#x02013;AMFPI (scintillator HARP active matrix flat panel imager). Med Phys 32:2954&#x02013;966 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16266110</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="other">Rauch P (2005) Fluoroscopy acceptance testing: technical considerations for image quality and dose. Presentation at the 2005 AAPM Annual Meeting, Seattle, WA. <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://aapm.org/meetings/05AM/PRAbs.asp?mid=18&#x00026;aid=2628">http://aapm.org/meetings/05AM/PRAbs.asp?mid=18&#x00026;aid=2628</ext-link>. Accessed 19 Jan 2006</citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Balter</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Shope</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><source>Intervascular brachytherapy/fluoroscopically guided interventions. Medical Physics Monograph # 28</source><year>2002</year><publisher-loc>Madison, Wis</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Medical Physics Publishing</publisher-name></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Balter S, Chan R, Shope T (2002) Intervascular brachytherapy/fluoroscopically guided interventions. Medical Physics Monograph no. 28. Medical Physics Publishing, Madison </citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>